    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find an expression for the sum\n$$1+2+2^2+\\cdots+2^{n-1}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2^n-1$",
          "worked": "The first term is $1$, the common ratio is $2$, and there are $n$ terms.\n$$\\begin{align*}S_n&=\\frac{1(2^n-1)}{2-1}\\\\S_n&=2^n-1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find an expression for the sum\n$$(1\\cdot1)+(2\\cdot2)+(3\\cdot2^2)+\\cdots+(n\\cdot2^{n-1}).$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(n-1)2^n+1$\n\nDouble the sum and subtract the original sum; use part (a) for the remaining geometric series.",
          "worked": "Let $T_n$ denote the required sum.\n$$\\begin{align*}T_n&=1\\cdot1+2\\cdot2+3\\cdot2^2+\\cdots+n\\cdot2^{n-1}\\\\2T_n&=1\\cdot2+2\\cdot2^2+3\\cdot2^3+\\cdots+n\\cdot2^n.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract the original sum from its double. The overlapping coefficients differ by $-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}T_n&=2T_n-T_n\\\\T_n&=-1-2-2^2-\\cdots-2^{n-1}+n2^n\\\\T_n&=-(1+2+2^2+\\cdots+2^{n-1})+n2^n\\\\T_n&=-(2^n-1)+n2^n\\\\T_n&=(n-1)2^n+1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      }
    ]
  },
